# Elm compilation output + sidecar fingerprints. The compiled kernel
# JS is generated by `scripts/build-elm.sh` against this tree's
# tracked Elm sources. The `.sha256` sidecars are emitted alongside
# so the build orchestrator can verify the produced JS byte-for-byte
# before staging it into the dogfood artifact.
#
# ACT-CLINEMM-P0-COMPLETION-CONTINUATION-CONTROL-AUTHORITY01-CORRECTION06:
# Unlike completion-authority/ and task-header-orchestration/ (which
# track `vendor/elm` for hermetic local builds), this kernel
# EXCLUDES `vendor/elm` from its commits per the factory review
# directive for CORRECTION06 ("Commit the full CORRECTION05+06+Elm
# substrate set, excluding vendor/elm"). The 60 MB duplicate is
# NOT carried in the repo; the build pipeline resolves the compiler
# from the global environment / a future centralization ACT.
# `.gitignore` keeps `vendor/elm` excluded; `.gitkeep` preserves
# the directory so tracked tools can populate it at build time.
vendor/*.js
vendor/*.js.sha256
vendor/elm
vendor/elm.sha256
vendor/elm.gz
vendor/elm.version
elm-stuff/
.elm-home/